WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.372
"NeuPL makes three contributions.

00:00:03.452 --> 00:00:06.823
First,

00:00:06.903 --> 00:00:10.275
it is a single conditional model that represents a
whole population of policies,

00:00:10.355 --> 00:00:13.727
conditioned on a meta-game mixture strategy that
specifies which opponents each policy should beat.

00:00:13.807 --> 00:00:17.178
Second,

00:00:17.258 --> 00:00:20.630
it is a unifying framework: by choosing the
interaction graph you recover self-play,

00:00:20.710 --> 00:00:24.082
fictitious play, or PSRO-Nash as special cases,

00:00:24.162 --> 00:00:27.533
and you can even express cyclic graphs that PSRO cannot.

00:00:27.613 --> 00:00:30.985
Third, it comes with convergence guarantees for grounded,

00:00:31.065 --> 00:00:34.437
lower-triangular interaction graphs and a suitable
meta-graph solver,

00:00:34.517 --> 00:00:37.888
NeuPL provably converges to an N-step best-response
and, with large enough N,

00:00:37.968 --> 00:00:41.340
to a normal-form Nash equilibrium."
